    [releases/v0.30.0][Attention][BugFix] Handle empty MLA PCP prefill ranks (#18195)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #17972 to `releases/v0.30.0`. This author-submitted PR replaces
    the bot-created backport #18189 with the same code patch.
    
    PCP can assign zero real prefill tokens to a rank while retaining padded
    KV inputs for collective processing. MLA preprocessing then attempts
    `prefill_k_pe.view(0, num_kv_heads, -1)` and raises an ambiguous
    zero-element reshape error. Use the existing `self.qk_rope_head_dim`
    instead of inferring the final dimension, preserving padded KV
    processing, collectives and the existing attention path.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. MLA PCP requests with a locally empty prefill rank can proceed
    through preprocessing instead of failing on the reshape. No API or
    configuration changes are introduced.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified that the backport patch matches merged #17972 and bot-created
    #18189. Both changed files are identical to #18189, and `git diff
    --check` passed.
    - Existing #18189 CI passed the full CPU unit tests with both the
    [verified vLLM main
    commit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38030570140/job/114151340151)
    and [vLLM
    v0.30.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38030570140/job/114151340147).
    [Pre-commit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38030570140/job/114150451875)
    also passed.
    - The regression test in `tests/ut/attention/test_mla_v1.py` covers 0, 1
    and 3 real local tokens, retained padded KV input and returned Q/K/V
    shapes.
    - Original validation in #17972 used BF16 DeepSeek-V2-Lite on
    Ascend950DT with MRV2, TP1/DCP1, PCP1/PCP2 and `enable_mlapo=false`.
    Empty-rank inference and the length boundary matrix matched output
    tokens across PCP1/PCP2 eager and PCP2 `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`; restoring the
    original line reproduced the reshape failure. The 35 selected
    prefill/preprocess unit tests passed.
    - The earlier NPU-backed whole-file unit-test run retained eight
    pre-existing failures and timed out during shutdown; that run is not
    claimed passing. Fused MLA prolog, prefill graph, MTP, prefix caching,
    async scheduling, quantized MLA, other PCP/DCP topologies and
    performance were outside that runtime validation.
    - CI for this resubmission is pending. No new NPU runtime validation was
    performed on this release backport.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
